  "id": "phonemic-awareness",
  "term": "phonemic awareness",
  "definition": "Phonemic awareness is the ability to notice and work with the individual speech sounds in spoken words. In the source, it is described as an early skill that develops alongside basic letter knowledge before reading and can shape how finely children process sound differences in speech.",
